# An HTTP/2 stream.
#
# NAMED GAP: SERVER PUSH IS NOT IMPLEMENTED, on any backend, and that is a decision rather than an omission.
# Chrome removed push support in 2022 and Firefox followed; hyper has never offered it server-side, Hummingbird
# does not, and Ktor's Netty engine does not expose it. Implementing it on node alone would be an API that means
# something on one backend of four, which is the thing this whole surface exists to avoid.
#
# `http2-push` therefore exists, answers false everywhere, and says why. It is here so that a program written
# against it compiles on every target and can be told at run time that the answer is no, rather than failing to
# resolve a name on three of them.
#
# Internal: reached only through the public network/http2 API.

load @term/seed/code/network/server/request
  find request

load @term/seed/code/native/node/network/http2/shared/request
  find http2-stream

# the stream a request arrived on, as text. 0 when the backend does not report one.
task http2-stream-of
  take request, like request
  like text
  send back
    call http2-stream
      read request

# Push `path` to the client ahead of its asking. Answers FALSE on every backend: see the gap above. Check the
# answer rather than assuming the push happened.
task http2-push
  take request, like request
  take path, like text
  like boolean
  send back, false
